# "How I get from question to shipped"
process:
  - word: Understand
    title: Start with the real problem
    text: >-
      I talk to the people who use the product and the people who build it before I draw anything.
      The brief is rarely the problem, so I write the problem down first and get everyone to agree on it.
    badges: [Interviews, Problem framing, Constraints]
  - word: Design
    title: Make it concrete early
    text: >-
      I move from sketches to clickable screens quickly, then put them in front of real users.
      Small, honest prototypes find the bad ideas while they are still cheap to change.
    badges: [Prototyping, Usability testing, Design systems]
  - word: Deliver
    title: Stay until it ships
    text: >-
      I work with engineers in code review, not only at handoff. Spacing, states and edge cases get
      settled in the build, so what you see in the design is what ships.
    badges: [Handoff, Front-end review, QA]

